{
  "_why": [
    "The presets demo mode pretends the unit is holding.",
    "",
    "Demo mode existed so somebody with no FM3 could see the app work, and for",
    "a long time it showed one preset with one chain and 511 empty slots. Every",
    "screen that reads a LIST — the preset list, the setlists, the scene tiles —",
    "was therefore being demonstrated empty, which is the one thing a demo must",
    "not do.",
    "",
    "So this is twelve presets that look like a working rig. Every amp, cab and",
    "drive number here is a real model on a real FM3, taken from the same",
    "rosters the app already ships (src/data/amp-types.json and its neighbours),",
    "not invented — a demo that names an amp nobody makes teaches the wrong",
    "thing.",
    "",
    "Each preset carries FOUR named scenes that actually differ: which blocks",
    "are off, which channel the amp is on, and where the levels sit. A scene",
    "list whose entries are identical is the same failure as an empty list, one",
    "step later.",
    "",
    "`chain` is the blocks in signal order. Only the slugs the mock's LAYOUT",
    "knows may appear, because those effect ids were captured off hardware and",
    "the block catalogue is built from them. `levels` is in dB for the amp and",
    "for anything whose Level is in dB; `off` is by slug, not effect id, so this",
    "file stays readable.",
    "",
    "A LEVEL BELONGS TO A CHANNEL, NOT TO A SCENE, and that is why every scene",
    "here selects a different amp channel. The first draft of this file gave two",
    "scenes the same channel and different levels; the second one silently won,",
    "because that is what the hardware does — a scene chooses a channel and the",
    "channel holds the value. Blocks a scene does not switch keep one setting",
    "for the whole preset, under `levels` on the preset rather than on a scene."
  ],
